𝐇𝐨𝐰 𝐀𝐧𝐬𝐢𝐛𝐥𝐞 𝐏𝐥𝐚𝐲𝐛𝐨𝐨𝐤𝐬 𝐀𝐮𝐭𝐨𝐦𝐚𝐭𝐞 𝐋𝐢𝐧𝐮𝐱

𝐀𝐧𝐬𝐢𝐛𝐥𝐞 𝐏𝐥𝐚𝐲𝐛𝐨𝐨𝐤𝐬 are at the heart of automation in Linux.
They use simple YAML syntax to define tasks, roles, and configurations.

Example:

- name: Install and start Apache
 hosts: webservers
 become: yes
 tasks:
 - name: Install Apache
 apt: name=apache2 state=present
 - name: Start Apache
 service: name=apache2 state=started


✅ No manual steps
✅ Repeatable, consistent configurations
✅ Scalable across multiple servers

Playbooks turn complex admin tasks into one-click automation.
